### Critical Mismatch Found
I have identified a significant mismatch between the **Tool Names** (used in UI/Registry) and the **Map Keys** in `N8nAiService.ts`. Because of this, many tools are currently **falling back to local execution** instead of using your n8n agents.

| UI/Registry Tool Name (`toolName`) | n8n Map Key (`N8N_FLOW_MAP`) | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `'grammar-checker'` | `'grammarCheck'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'ai-detector'` | `'detectAi'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'bias-checker'` | `'biasCheck'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'fact-checker'` | `'factCheck'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'plagiarism-checker'` | `'plagiarismCheck'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'ai-researcher'` | `'aiResearch'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'lecture-generator'` | `'generateLecture'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'generate-toc'` | `'generateTOC'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'generate-ui-description'`| `'generateUIDescription'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'generate-session-plan'` | `'generateSessionPlan'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'solve-assignments'` | `'solveAssignments'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'generate-project-blueprint'`| `'generateProjectBlueprint'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'summarizer'` | `'summarize'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |
| `'paraphraser'` | `'paraphrase'` | ❌ **Mismatch** (Runs locally) |

### Analysis of the Impact
When you click "Grammar Checker" in the UI:
1.  `RunAiToolUseCase` is called with `toolName: 'grammar-checker'`.
2.  It calls `N8nAiService.runFlow(..., 'grammar-checker')`.
3.  `N8nAiService` looks for `this.N8N_FLOW_MAP['grammar-checker']`.
4.  **It finds nothing** (since the key is `grammarCheck`), so it prints `Running flow locally: grammar-checker` and uses the local Genkit flow instead of your n8n agent.

### Recommended Fix
The `N8N_FLOW_MAP` keys should be updated to match the tool IDs exactly as they appear in the `ToolProviders`.

**Would you like me to:**
1.  **Generate a corrected version of the `N8N_FLOW_MAP`** that uses the actual hyphenated tool names as keys?
2.  **Verify if your n8n agents** expect the camelCase name (`grammarCheck`) or the hyphenated name (`grammar-checker`) in the `flowName` field of the JSON payload?
3.  **Check other modules** to see if this naming inconsistency affects other parts of the system?
